 "result_text": "Equation fields now use Knack's formatted value for `.formatted`, so your example should give 4 (days) instead of 372171.318 (seconds). I haven't run the tests or tried it on a real record.\n\n- **The fix:** I added `\"equation\": {\"use_knack_format\": True}` to `FIELD_SETTINGS` in `knackpy/models.py`. `.raw` still holds the `_raw` value.\n- **Extra change:** In `knackpy/fields.py`, `Field._format` used `if self.knack_formatted_value`, which would have ignored a formatted value of `0` and fallen back to the raw one. I changed it to `is not None`. That check applies to every field type that uses the Knack format, not only equations.\n- **No new formatter:** The issue suggested adding a function to the formatter module. I didn't, because equation fields already fall through to `default()`, which returns the value unchanged.",
